.clinerules for `music_app`

Scope
- This is a Flutter app using a hybrid layered architecture with feature-based presentation organization.
- Only change files directly related to the requested task. Do not refactor unrelated areas.
- Do not create new architectural styles if the existing project already has a clear place for the change.

Architecture To Preserve
- Primary state management is `flutter_bloc` with `Bloc`/`Cubit` in `lib/presentation/bloc/`.
- Dependency injection uses `get_it` in `lib/core/di/service_locator.dart`.
- The codebase follows a clean-ish layered split:
  - `lib/domain/`: entities, repository contracts, use cases.
  - `lib/data/`: models, repository implementations, mapping to Supabase/Hive.
  - `lib/presentation/bloc/`: state management per feature.
  - `lib/pages/` + `lib/widgets/`: UI.
  - `lib/services/`: cross-cutting services such as audio, auth, lyrics, storage.
  - `lib/core/`: config, constants, DI, router, errors, utilities.
- Keep the existing hybrid approach: some features go through domain/data layers, while some app-specific behavior talks to Supabase directly from Cubits/Services. Do not force full clean architecture unless explicitly requested.

State Management Rules
- Prefer adding logic to an existing `Bloc`/`Cubit` when the feature already has one.
- New stateful business logic should usually live in `lib/presentation/bloc/<feature>/`.
- Keep state classes in dedicated `*_state.dart` files and events in `*_event.dart` for Bloc-based features.
- Use `Equatable` for state/value classes when the surrounding feature already uses it.
- Do not introduce Riverpod, GetX, MobX, Redux, or another state solution.

Dependency Injection Rules
- Register shared dependencies via `get_it` in `lib/core/di/service_locator.dart`.
- Match existing lifetimes:
  - `registerLazySingleton` for shared app-wide services/cubits already treated as singletons.
  - `registerFactory` for short-lived feature cubits/use cases currently created per usage.
- Do not bypass DI for reusable services if the same kind of dependency is already resolved from `getIt`.

Data And Domain Rules
- Repository contracts belong in `lib/domain/repositories/`.
- Repository implementations belong in `lib/data/repositories/`.
- Entities belong in `lib/domain/entities/`.
- DTO/model mapping belongs in `lib/data/models/`.
- When a feature already has a use case, keep orchestration there instead of pushing extra logic into UI.
- Preserve existing local/remote split: Hive for local persistence/cache, Supabase for backend/auth/storage/RPC.

UI And Feature Placement
- Full screens go in `lib/pages/<feature>/`.
- Shared or reusable UI components go in `lib/widgets/` or feature subfolders under `lib/pages/`.
- Keep admin-specific UI under `lib/pages/admin/`, auth under `lib/pages/auth/`, player under `lib/pages/player/`, and so on.
- Avoid moving files across folders unless the task explicitly requires restructuring.

Naming Conventions
- File names use `snake_case.dart`.
- Classes, enums, typedefs use `PascalCase`.
- Variables, parameters, methods, and fields use `camelCase`.
- Private members use a leading underscore.
- Keep existing suffix conventions:
  - `*Cubit`, `*Bloc`, `*State`, `*Event`
  - `*Repository`, `*RepositoryImpl`
  - `*UseCase` / `*Usecase` only match the local feature's existing spelling
  - `*Entity`, `*Model`, `*Page`, `*Service`

Code Style Rules
- Follow the current Dart/Flutter style in the touched file before applying personal preferences.
- Keep imports package-relative when that file already uses package imports; otherwise preserve existing relative style nearby.
- Favor small, targeted edits over large rewrites.
- Add comments only when the logic is non-obvious; keep them short.
- Do not rename symbols, reorder files, or mass-format unrelated code.

Editing Discipline
- Before editing, inspect the nearest related files to mirror local patterns.
- Keep changes scoped to the feature being requested.
- If a task touches audio, auth, Supabase, playlists, or admin flows, verify the existing service/cubit/repository path before changing code.
- Respect current initialization order in `lib/main.dart`: Hive -> Supabase -> service locator -> preload/setup -> `runApp`.

Testing And Validation
- Prefer adding or updating tests only when they are directly relevant to the requested change.
- Use the existing test structure under `test/unit/`, `test/widget/`, and `test/integration/`.
- Do not create speculative tests for untouched features.

Avoid
- Do not introduce a new architecture layer without a strong project-specific reason.
- Do not spread a simple change across many folders if one existing feature file is enough.
- Do not modify secrets/config unless explicitly requested.
- Do not edit unrelated files just to make style more "perfect".

UI And Design Standards
- Always read and follow DESIGN_SKILL.md before creating or editing any UI widget, page, or component.
- Apply the design principles in DESIGN_SKILL.md for typography, colors, spacing, animations, and visual effects.
- Do not create generic or plain UI — every screen must follow the design tone defined in DESIGN_SKILL.md.

Never re-read the same file more than once per task.
Never explain why tools are not working — just retry once, 
then continue with available information.
Do not ask the user to paste file contents.